# Static files first.
/robots.txt     /robots.txt     200
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap.xml    200

# Every app route is prerendered to its own flat .html file at build time, so these
# rewrites point straight at the built file.
#
# Note the flat files: emitting `directory/index.html` instead makes Cloudflare Pages
# answer a request for `/directory` with a 308 to `/directory/`. That redirect used to
# collide with the rewrite for the same path and send visitors to `/`, silently
# discarding the path, so every deep link landed on the homepage.
#
# Anything not listed here falls through to 404.html with a real 404 status, rather
# than the old behaviour where every junk URL returned 200 with the homepage (a
# 'soft 404' that pollutes search results).
#
# If you add a route, add it to src/lib/nav.tsx, src/lib/routes.ts, and here.
# `npm run build` fails if those three disagree.

/                /index.html     200
/directory       /directory.html 200
/partners        /partners.html  200
/about           /about.html     200
/feedback        /feedback.html  200
/give            /give.html      200
/guide           /guide.html     200
/volunteer       /volunteer.html 200
/impact          /impact.html    200
/join            /join.html      200
/contact         /contact.html   200
/privacy         /privacy.html   200
/terms           /terms.html     200

# /donate was a thin duplicate of /give with no inbound links. A 301 consolidates the
# two so search engines index one page instead of two competing ones.
/donate          /give           301
